===============
| Java Arrays |
===============
👉An array is a data structure that stores multiple values of the same data type in a single variable.

int[] marks = {90, 85, 78, 92, 88};

  👉 Stores multiple values.
  👉 Stores same data type only.
  👉 Index starts from 0.
  👉 Fixed size.
  👉 Stored in contiguous memory (conceptually for Java arrays).
  👉 Faster access using index.

datatype[] arrayName = new datatype[size];

int[] numbers = new int[5];                   int[] numbers = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};    // Array Initialization
int numbers[] = new int[5];

numbers → array name
int → data type
5 → size
-----------------------------------
int[] numbers = new int[5];   // Assigning Values
numbers[0] = 10;
numbers[1] = 20;
numbers[2] = 30;
numbers[3] = 40;
numbers[4] = 50;
